      "title": "Disparity refinement: what each prior gets right",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "DISPARITY REFINEMENT - one raw SGBM map, six ways to clean it up.\n\nRow 1 is the baseline: SGBM leaves holes wherever the scene has no texture, which on a driving scene is the road surface and the sky.\n\nRow 2, WLS: the same SGBM run in BOTH directions, consistency-checked, then smoothed along the left image's edges. It fills the holes and it outputs a confidence map, which is the thing to keep. What it does NOT do is respect a slanted surface: its prior is fronto-parallel, so a plane fit through the road band goes from 0.06 m RMS / 98% inliers on the RAW map to 0.36 m / 33% after the filter. It corrupts pixels the matcher already had right - lowering wls_lambda only trades that against coverage.\n\nRow 3, 'CV Disparity Filter (WLS)': the same filter applied to a map it did not produce - here StereoBM's, which starts at 71% valid on this pair and comes back at 88%. Set num_disparities / min_disparity / block_size to match the matcher that made the map: they place the region to filter and pick depth_discontinuity_radius, and being wrong about either moves the result by 2000+ px. Without disparity_right there is no left-right check, so 'confidence' comes back as zeros.\n\nRow 4, RIC interpolation: fits a local AFFINE model per superpixel instead of a constant one - which is exactly what a road is - so it fills the same holes without bending the ground. This is the one to use in front of a point cloud.\n\nRows 5-6 (blue), the generic edge-aware smoothers that are already in the pack as generated nodes: guidedFilter and fastGlobalSmootherFilter (the FGS the WLS filter is built on). Note what they do with the holes: neither has any notion of an INVALID pixel, so the -1 marker is averaged into its neighbourhood like a real measurement.\n\nNot shown, because it cannot run here: ximgproc.fastBilateralSolverFilter, the textbook confidence-driven depth filler, raises '(-213) needs to be compiled with EIGEN' on this OpenCV build. Also available as generated nodes: getDisparityVis (the canonical disparity visualization), weightedMedianFilter (speckle cleanup), filterSpeckles and validateDisparity.\n\nTry: drop wls_lambda to 100 and watch WLS stop filling; raise superpixel_size and watch RIC start ignoring thin structures."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
